3:  *
4:  * Desktop (mouse + wide screen): the slow 360° spin is a CSS animation
5:  * (kzLogoSpin in scroll-3d.css) that runs on the GPU, and this script only adds
6:  * the scroll / mouse tilt. Its animation loop runs while the logo is still
7:  * easing towards the new position and then stops, so an idle page does no work.
8:  *
9:  * Phones, tablets and "reduce motion": the logo stays still. The old version
10:  * re-rendered the logo 60 times a second for as long as the page was open,
11:  * which made scrolling stutter on phones and drained the battery.
